{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "All four completed experiments use singleprofile, leaving the single-vs-multiprofile question completely untested. The best singleprofile result is config_008 (scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) at 0.5362 acc. Config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the most controlled extension: it keeps the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy, and introduces only the profile change plus the minimal aggregation (avgpool) that multiprofile requires. This isolates whether multiple profiles contribute useful signal beyond a single profile. If multiprofile with simple averaging matches or beats 0.5362, it justifies investing in more complex aggregation (transformer) and other multiprofile variants; if it falls well short, it tells us the extra profiles add noise and we should focus budget on singleprofile refinements (e.g., fusion type, image encoder). This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design axis remaining, making it the best use of the next limited experiment."
}

